title: Moving between genres
intro: A platformer level plays a match-3 board on top of itself as a minigame and hears how it went; a door joins the level to a cave both ways; and the level remembers how it was left.
project: Platformer | Genre Trip

chapter: A minigame scene | A board that's won on its first match
menu: File > New Scene...
prompt: Arcade
create: Match Board
set: MatchBoard.Seed = 152
add: Trigger
set: Trigger.Message = Match
set: Trigger.Do = Win Minigame
expectvalue: Board.Trigger.Do = Win Minigame
explain: field:Trigger.Do | Win Minigame | A trigger in the minigame ends it. Here the board's first match wins it, with the board's score; Lose Minigame loses it.
save

chapter: Played from the level | A Minigame on the checkpoint flag
scene: Main
select: Checkpoint
set: Checkpoint.Message = Reached
add: Minigame
pick: Minigame.Scene = Arcade
explain: field:Minigame.PauseBelow | Pause Below | A Minigame plays another scene on top of this one. It takes the screen and the player's input, and pauses the rest of the level while it's played.
add: Trigger
set: Trigger.Message = Reached
set: Trigger.Do = Play
expectvalue: Checkpoint.Trigger.Do = Play
explain: field:Trigger.Do | Play | Reaching the flag plays it.
select: Score
add: Trigger
set: Trigger.Message = Minigame Won
set: Trigger.Do = Add
set: Trigger.UseMessageNumber = true
explain: component:Trigger | Minigame Won | When it's won, the flag sends Minigame Won with the score, and this trigger adds it to the level's score.
play
hold: Right 1.4
wait: 1
expectvalue: Checkpoint.Minigame.Playing = true
expectvalue: Player.PlatformerMovement.Controllable = false
explain: game | The minigame has the screen | The match board was loaded into the level, beside it, and has the screen and the input. The level waits, paused.
gameclick: Board + 3.5, -1.5
wait: 0.3
gameclick: Board + 4.5, -1.5
wait: 2
expectvalue: Checkpoint.Minigame.Won = true
expectvalue: Checkpoint.Minigame.Playing = false
expectvalue: Player.PlatformerMovement.Controllable = true
explain: game | Back in the level | The first match won it. The board is gone, the player has the input again, and the score came back with the message.
stop

chapter: A door to a cave and back | Arrive At, and a level that remembers
menu: File > New Scene...
prompt: Cave
agent: entity_create {"entities": [{"name": "Floor", "position": [0, -4.5], "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#4A4E5A", "size": [40, 1]}, "BoxCollider": {"size": [40, 1]}}}, {"name": "Cave Entrance", "position": [-6, -3.5]}, {"name": "Way Back", "position": [-3, -3.25], "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#8A5A3A", "size": [1, 1.5]}, "BoxCollider": {"isTrigger": true, "size": [1, 1.5]}, "Door": {"scene": "Main", "arriveAt": "Cave Door", "fade": 0.3}}}]}
save
scene: Main
agent: entity_create {"entity": {"name": "Cave Door", "position": [2.5, -3.25], "components": {"Sprite": {"tint": "#8A5A3A", "size": [3, 1.5]}, "BoxCollider": {"isTrigger": true, "size": [3, 1.5]}, "Door": {"fade": 0.3, "needsInteract": true}}}}
select: Cave Door
pick: Door.Scene = Cave
choose: Door.Arrive At:choice = Cave Entrance
expectvalue: Cave Door.Door.ArriveAt = Cave Entrance
explain: field:Door.Arrive At | Arrive At | A door to another scene says where you arrive there, picked from that scene's entities. The cave's own door arrives back here, at this one, so they join both ways.
select: Player
add: Keep Between Scenes
explain: component:KeepBetweenScenes | Keep Between Scenes | The player goes along, with their hearts, into the cave and back.
select: Level
add: Remember Scene
explain: component:RememberScene | Remember Scene | And the level remembers how it was left: coming back, it's as it was, not as the scene file has it.
save
play
hold: Right 1.4
wait: 1
gameclick: Board + 3.5, -1.5
wait: 0.3
gameclick: Board + 4.5, -1.5
wait: 2
expectvalue: Checkpoint.Minigame.Wins = 1
say: The minigame is won once more, and by the flag is the door to the cave. E goes through.
tap: E
wait: 1.2
expectvalue: Player.Transform.Position.X = -6 ~ 0.3
explain: game | In the cave | The player arrives at the cave's entrance, carried along.
hold: Right 1
wait: 1.5
expectvalue: Player.Transform.Position.X = 3 ~ 3
expectvalue: Checkpoint.Checkpoint.Active = true
expectvalue: Checkpoint.Minigame.Playing = false
expectvalue: Checkpoint.Minigame.Wins = 1
explain: game | Back, as it was left | Back through the cave's door, they arrive at the level's. The level is as it was left: the flag was reached already, so the minigame doesn't start again, and it still counts its win.
stop
